      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "**Noire** (2011) marked a fascinating neo-noir experiment that sadly got lost in the indie festival circuit. Director Marcus Chen crafted a deliberately disorienting thriller that pays homage to classics like <a href=\"/movie/996\" class=\"movie-title\">Double Indemnity</a> (1944) while incorporating elements of Asian horror reminiscent of **Dark Water** (2002). The film's high-contrast black and white photography and unreliable narrator structure draws clear inspiration from **Memento** (2000), though its execution feels more experimental and less commercially polished."
      },
