      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Chen's background in Asian cinema clearly influences **Noire** (2011), particularly in its supernatural undertones. The film shares DNA with Korean noir thrillers like **Oldboy** (2003) and **The Chaser** (2008), while its ghost story elements echo Japanese horror-noir hybrids like **Dark Water** (2002) and **Cure** (1997)."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film's unconventional structure, with its nested flashbacks and unreliable narration, feels particularly indebted to complex Asian noir like **Infernal Affairs** (2002) and **A Bittersweet Life** (2005). Yet Chen filters these influences through a distinctly American indie sensibility reminiscent of early Christopher Nolan works like **Following** (1998)."
      }
